WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
There is a colonial woman on the wing.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.320
She is dressed in
traditional colonial garb!

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.640
Get off!

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.560
It's possible for people to
grab hold of the intercom,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.000
but we have special codes to be able to

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.520
get our voice across.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.000
Hi, I'm Kristine Fernandez.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.520
I was an international flight attendant

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.040
for a premium airline
for about seven years.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.680
I was based in Dubai

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.040
and have experience working in first class

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.800
and as a senior leading the cabin crew.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.440
Today, I'll be looking at
flight-attendant scenes

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.280
from movies and judging how real they are.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.000
from movies and judging how real they are.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.960
Come aboard, Mr. Young, Miss Chu.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.760
Here's the way to your private suite.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.280
And some Champagne.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.160
I love this one!

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.480
I felt like that was the
airline that I worked for.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.320
So, the bar that they walk into, you know,

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.360
that's almost exactly what it looked like.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.160
So that for us would be
the business-class bar.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.000
First class is insane.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.680
You have your own private suite

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.160
where the doors close automatically,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.400
and the best part is the shower.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.080
Yes, there is a shower spa.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.240
In order to use that,
you have allocated time.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.400
So it's 30 minutes,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.760
and the flight attendants would go ahead

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.520
and set up the spa for you

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.480
so that all the towels are warm.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.280
The floors are heated.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.880
The floors are heated in
your shower spa on the plane.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.040
So it's pretty wild.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.920
And there's, like, a
refreshment drink afterwards.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.680
It's very beautiful.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.520
Nick, we can't afford this!

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.760
These pajamas are fancier
than any of my real clothes.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.840
So, we hand out pajamas,
you have slippers.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.760
So you have a small amenities kit,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.640
which is, like, this size.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:37.520
You have your toothbrush,

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.720
you have your socks and eye shades.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.440
I think 10 out of 10.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.120
Honestly, when I was
watching that bar scene,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.480
I felt like I was back at —

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.040
I was like, oh, I know those people.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.480
That's book's messy.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.160
What's wrong with messy?

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.520
The first thing about that
clip that stood out to me

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.680
you wouldn't believe
was actually the hair,

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.600
because the uniform standards
of flight attendants

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.160
is so very specific,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.760
especially for the airline
that I worked with.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.560
So, all hair must be back, right?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.000
So if it's shoulder-length hair

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.720
and it's not touching the shoulders,

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.680
you can have it down.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.000
But anything longer than that,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.160
then you have to have up,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.680
definitely away from the face,

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.080
with a maximum of six bobby pins.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.440
The reason why hair was up

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.120
was more from a hygiene perspective,

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.720
because you're in food service.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.560
In the event of an emergency,

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.440
having your hair up is good.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.720
So when the hair was out here,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.440
I was like, not so much.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.680
The way that most flight
attendants see the lavatory

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.680
is like it's a public toilet in dry air.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.040
So it's like the least sexiest place

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.600
that anything can really go down.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.360
Getting steamy in the
public toilet in the air

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.760
is very undesirable.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.320
For most. For most.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.240
But not ruling it out for everyone.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.280
Will you have dinner with me?

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.840
OK, that was, like, a supercute moment,

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.000
but I'm really not
supposed to do that, so.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.720
OK, well, Bangkok
can be really magical.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.120
First of all,

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.840
having a cute passenger on board

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.360
that you're just like, mew, mew, mew,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.640
quite rare.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.480
But also to have that open flirtation

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.080
in the middle of the aisles,

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.840
probably someone on the side being like,

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.400
"Excuse me, can I have a drink?"

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.960
Or, "Excuse me, here's some rubbish."

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.320
So that flirtation, if
it were to really happen,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.600
it would happen more in the galley,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.280
because it's more quiet

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.800
and you can just sort
of chat with each other,

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.400
but definitely flirtation
can happen on the plane.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.040
I used to get asked

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.960
if I would like to marry someone.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.400
Someone once asked me, they were like,

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.640
"Give me your number, please."

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.760
And I was like, "I don't
think that's appropriate.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.000
Would you like a drink instead?"

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.440
And then they were like, "I
promise I will call you."

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.240
And I'm like,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.440
that's exactly why I'm
not giving you my number.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.520
Maybe, like, a 6 out of 10.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.120
There were a lot of things
happening in one scene

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.120
which may happen in different scenarios.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.200
Miss, you cannot be up here.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.000
Hello, Grandpa.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.760
I'm sorry, I just want to
be here with my friends.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.920
How often do we have to
deal with drunk passengers?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.400
All the time. Pretty much every flight.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.960
One of the cabins that we had

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.720
had a whole bar in it.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.520
There would be people who would
do the whole entire flight,

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.360
13 to 14 hours, just at the bar.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.720
We've had dancing.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.200
We've had people go from, like,

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.560
being the quietest passengers

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.680
at the beginning of the flight to,

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.760
by the end of the hours of drinking

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.000
is like everyone's best friend,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.560
inviting everyone to the holiday

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.920
that they're about to go to.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.920
Passengers are not allowed
up here in first class.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.120
It's policy. I'm sorry.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.000
That's very true.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.240
That's how strict it is.
Like, that's how real it is.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.640
Miss.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.680
Um, no, it's not me.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.760
In the night flights, we walk
through the different cabins

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.360
just to check how everything is.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.560
There were a lot of seats, and these guys

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.680
pretty much made their way into there

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.040
and then covered themselves in blankets

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.760
and basically did their whole
flight as business class.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.640
It's not allowed, but it can happen.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.760
Whatever you say, Stove.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.440
It's Steve.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.680
The touching is definitely not allowed.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.560
Does it happen?

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.920
Sometimes, but we're really firm.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.440
We're very stern,

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.000
because that's definitely
crossing the line.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.040
So it's a direct confrontation
of, "That's not acceptable."

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.640
And if it continues —

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.600
it's never continued, so I've
never gone to that level.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.840
I have an announcement too.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.600
There is a colonial woman on the wing.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.640
She is dressed in
traditional colonial garb!

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.040
Get off!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.000
It's possible for people to
grab hold of the intercom.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.080
It's knowing what buttons to press.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.520
10 out of 10, plus more.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.360
I can imagine it happening in real life.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.440
[pilot grunting]

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.040
What the hell?!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.120
Never would that happen,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.240
but I did once get sent a photo

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.960
of a snake being on a plane.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:17.960
I don't know where it came from,

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.000
but someone said, "This was on my flight.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.760
And there was just a little,
little friendly little snake.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.400
But never, not at this level.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.920
One thing that you can expect

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.000
on a flight in first class

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.680
is a falcon.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.160
Was something that even we're trained for

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.880
on the airline that I worked with.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.520
Odd things happen on a plane.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.240
My flatmate, she
delivered a baby on board.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.240
On our flight, in all cabins,

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.840
everyone gets handed out
a hot towel to freshen up.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.320
And one time I handed out this towel,

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.720
the guy, like, he took it,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.560
and he just looked at me,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.960
and then he was like,

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.360
and I was like, "yeah," like, you know,

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.480
and he's like ...

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.000
[laughs]

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.880
Like, he ate the hot towel!

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.400
I couldn't believe it.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.560
What's up with the oxygen masks deploying?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.280
Oh, sorry about that.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.480
You're not gonna believe
what came out of the

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.320
[beep] instrument panel.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.160
Definitely if there's anything
to be concerned about,

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.960
you can just go straight to the cockpit.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.760
Like, anything emergency
1, just ring or go in.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.560
Most of the time if
there's heavy turbulence,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.720
the flight attendant
wouldn't be in the cockpit,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:31.880
the captain would say

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.760
"for all crews to take their seats."

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.080
So even at that level, no
crew would be walking around.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.040
So definitely, like,

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.760
a 0.5 out of 10.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:42.920
Attendant: Sir, you're
going to have to check that.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:43.840
Greg: I got it.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.120
Attendant: No, I'm sorry.
That bag won't fit.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.360
No, no, I'm not — hey!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.680
I'm not checking my bag. OK?

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.760
OK. There's no need to
raise your voice, sir.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:50.680
I'm not raising my voice.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.360
This would be raising my voice to you!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.320
This is 1,000% true.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.720
It happens all the time.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.480
I feel like I've had this exact
conversation with someone.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.520
But I will say the flight
attendant's composure here

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:06.520
is also very real. That's
what's expected of you.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.720
One time, I was still new.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.760
Can't really land until everyone's seated,

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.200
but one guy really wanted
to go to the toilet,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.520
and he kept on looking
at me like, "Can I go?"

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.160
And I was like, "No, you can't go."

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.120
He goes, "No, I'm going."

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.400
He brought, like,

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.480
he brought a plastic bag with him,

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.320
and he turned around,

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.520
and I didn't understand what he was doing.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.160
And then, as it turns out,

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:30.000
he urinated in the bag,
and then he tied it up,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.960
and then he put it in front of me.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.800
And, like, what do you do?

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.480
Did that just happen in my real life?

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.640
You know what? Get your grubby
little paws off of my bag!

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.000
OK? It's not like I have a bomb in here!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.160
It's not like I want to blow up the plane.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.000
Sir!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.000
I just want to stow my bag

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.760
according to your safety regulations!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.240
Even if what you're saying is a joke

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.680
or even if it's completely hypothetical,

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:53.840
like, he was just angry,

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.920
but that's something that

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.960
would cause a flight to
be definitely delayed.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.560
So if someone says that,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.880
everyone would definitely be deplaned.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.800
So there are some serious
repercussions around that.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.800
Giving it a 9 out of 10.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.800
I hear about it all the time,
I just never experienced it.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.600
Sometimes it might be in business class,

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.760
'cause the suites can be shared.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.120
One time, the guys in first class

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.720
rang all of the stations
just to let us know

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:34.720
that there was a couple
having sex in the shower spa.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.160
What?

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.080
Tom: Crapper's got my foot.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:40.080
Oh! OK, wait, let me help.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.080
OK. OK, one, two, three.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.720
The thing that stands out to me

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:47.920
is that's how small the toilet is.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.720
That's the kind of space that
you would be working with.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.400
That's the possible
things that could happen,

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.400
where your foot could actually
end up in the toilet bowl.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.800
Return to your seats now, please.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.440
Beat it, stew!

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.040
They can knock, knock, knock,

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.880
but there's, you know,
there's so much you can do.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:11.880
But I don't believe any
specific protocol around that.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.640
It would be like, "This is not safe,

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.120
because if turbulence happens, we can't,

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.400
two people can't be in the toilet,

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.120
let alone fasten seat
belts whilst, you know,"

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.640
so that's probably the angle
that it would come from.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.280
It's like, you can't just assume

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.480
and jump the gun and be like,

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.640
"Guys, no sex allowed."

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.360
You just, you kind of leave it.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.640
9 out of 10.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.960
There is an oxygen mask up above you,

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.200
on a hidden shelf.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.360
Before helping the people who love you,

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.640
put it on yourself.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.160
So, the fake planes, for us,

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.800
we called them the simulators.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:48.240
The overall setup of
it is pretty accurate.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.920
The tone here was more like, you know,

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.320
they're sitting there
waiting for it to happen.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.680
When you're in training college,
it's a bit more serious.

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.880
All of the tests, especially
the safety and security one,

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.760
they're known to be the
most stressful times.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.800
There are so many things
that you've got to remember

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.160
beyond just the commands.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.160
You've got to memorize things like,

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.760
how many doors are there?

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.760
Where are the fire extinguishers located?

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.320
They've got different
aircrafts to memorize.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.760
